<title>MAURITANIA: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>MAURITANIA GOVERNMENT LIST (970106)</p>
<p> *************************************************************</p>
<p> * 5 Jan 97  - President TAYA reshuffled the government with *</p>
<p> *		 Cheikh El Afia Ould Mohamed KHOUNA staying on *</p>
<p> *		 as prime minister.				    *</p>
<p> *************************************************************</p>
<p> President.....................Col Maaouya Ould Sid'Ahmed TAYA</p>
<p>				    (sworn in 18 Apr 92 for 6-yr term)</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>CABINET (Formed 20 April 1992, reshuffled 5 Jan 97): Prime Minister (Apptd 2 Jan</p>
<p>     96)....................Cheikh El Afia Ould Mohamed KHOUNA</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p>Civil Service, Labour,</p>
<p>     Youth &amp; Sports.............................Baba Ould SIDI</p>
<p>Communication (information) &amp;</p>
<p>     Parliamentary Relations.................Rachid Ould SALEH</p>
<p> Culture, Islamic Affairs.................Khattry ould GIDDREU</p>
<p> Defence.....................................Mohamed Ould AMAR</p>
<p> Education................................Sghairy Ould MBARACK</p>
<p> Finance...................................Camara Ali GUELADIO</p>
<p> Fisheries, Maritime Economy................Abdallahi Ould NEM</p>
<p> Foreign Affairs &amp; Cooperation...............Sidi Ould KHALIFA</p>
<p> Health, Social Affairs...........Mohamed Mahmoud Ould DAHMANE</p>
<p> Interior, Post &amp; Telecommunications........Kabbah Ould ELEWAH</p>
<p> Justice.......................Ethmane Ould Sid'Ahmed EL YESSA</p>
<p> Mining &amp; Industry........................N'gaide Lamine KAYOU</p>
<p> Planning..............................Ahmed Killy Ould CHEIKH</p>
<p>Rural Development &amp;</p>
<p>     Environment...........................Boidel Ould HOUMEID</p>
<p> Secretary-General of the Presidency.....Col Ahmed Ould MINNIH</p>
<p> Trade, Craft, &amp; Tourism........................SOW Abou Demba</p>
<p> Transport, Supplies.........................SOW Mohamed Deina</p>
<p> Water, Energy...........................Ahmed Yeslem Ould VIL</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Central Bank Governor.........................Ahmed Ould ZEIN</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>	 NOTE: Any comments/queries on the content of this</p>
<p>		 government list, please contact the Reuter</p>
<p>		 Editorial Reference Unit, London, on (171) 542</p>
<p>		 7968.</p>
<p>			  (End Government List)</p>
</text>
